🛡️ Security Operations Center (SOC)
The SOC is the nerve center for monitoring and defending an organization’s digital infrastructure.
Daily Tasks:
- Monitor network traffic and system logs for suspicious activity
- Respond to alerts from intrusion detection/prevention systems (IDS/IPS)
- Investigate potential security incidents and escalate as needed
- Maintain and tune SIEM (Security Information and Event Management) tools
- Coordinate with other departments to verify anomalies
- Conduct threat intelligence analysis and update detection rules
- Generate daily security reports and dashboards
- Perform vulnerability scans and track remediation efforts

🧑‍💻 DevSecOps
DevSecOps integrates security into the software development lifecycle, ensuring secure code and infrastructure from the start.
Daily Tasks:
- Review and scan code for vulnerabilities during development
- Automate security testing in CI/CD pipelines
- Collaborate with developers to fix security issues in code
- Monitor cloud configurations and infrastructure for compliance
- Update and manage security policies as code (e.g., IAM roles, firewall rules)
- Deploy and maintain automated security tools (e.g., SAST, DAST)
- Conduct threat modeling and risk assessments for new features
- Educate development teams on secure coding practices

🚨 Incident Response Team (CIRT / CSIRT / CERT)
This team is the first responder to cybersecurity incidents, ensuring swift containment and recovery.
Daily Tasks:
- Monitor incident queues and triage incoming reports
- Investigate alerts and determine scope and impact
- Coordinate containment and eradication efforts
- Document incident details and maintain response logs
- Communicate with affected stakeholders and leadership
- Update and test incident response playbooks
- Conduct post-incident reviews and recommend improvements
- Collaborate with legal and compliance teams for reporting obligations
